  "question": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> has highest boiling point among hydrogen halides, because it has:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "lowest dissociation enthalpy",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "strongest van der Waals’ interactions",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "strongest hydrogen bonding",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "lowest ionic character",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Boiling point is directly proportional to intermolecular Forces. Since Fluorine is highly electronegative element it forms hydrogen bonding. Because of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>-</mo></math> bonding <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> has high boiling point.<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0120_8173c5db851f.png\" /></p>"
  }
